    "done_when": "A test in tests/test_a_link_that_orders_nothing_is_named.py builds a fixture with a satisfied after edge and a satisfied depends_on edge to a closed plan, with no open waiting section, and asserts settled-link on both in wiring_findings at severity info, each naming the ref and the set that removes it; the same edges with an open section still waiting raise nothing, which is the control; and a fixture with A to B, B to C and A to C raises redundant-link on A to C only. On the base commit neither finding exists and the test fails there. The counts per mount go in the manifest. The negative control is executed and logged. Gate: tests/test_a_link_that_orders_nothing_is_named.py tests/test_graph_target.py tests/test_roadmap_endpoints.py tests/test_section_relations_count_as_wiring.py. baseline_suite and after_suite are run with the project's armed suite command, PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q tests/test_a_link_that_orders_nothing_is_named.py, at the base and at the head, each log naming its revision, tree and literal command and ending EXIT=. Every test file that imports a production module the node changed adds no failure against a base arm: run both arms from git archive extractions on node-local disk with the main checkout's .env linked, record both logs, and re-run any id that differs between arms serially three times on each revision. ruff check and ruff format --check add no findings on the staged paths. Run the gate in the foreground on the fleet allocation.",
